== Paste boost (optional) ==

Pound @?Thai basil leaves{15}(finely shredded) to a paste in a #mortar and pestle{}. Add @?fingerroot{1}(one piece) and pound again, then the @?fermented shrimp paste{1%tsp}. Pound the green curry paste into it before starting the curry.

> Or blend the basil, fingerroot and shrimp paste with some of the stock and add it with the stock.

== Curry ==

Boil the @coconut milk{3/4%cup} in a #heavy-bottomed pot{} over medium heat.

Add the @green curry paste{3 1/2%tbsp} and fry, stirring often, ~{3-5%minutes} until the oil separates. If it sticks, loosen it with a splash of the remaining coconut milk or stock.

Stir in the @chicken thigh{1%lb}.

Add the @chicken stock{1%cup}, @coconut milk{1%cup}, @palm sugar{2%tbsp} and @fish sauce{1%tbsp}. Bruise the @makrut lime leaves{5}, tear them into pieces without the stems, and add them. Simmer gently ~{10-15%minutes} until the chicken is tender.

Meanwhile cut the @Thai eggplant{1/2%lb} into bite-sized wedges and keep them in water.

Add the eggplant, pushing it under for the first minute so it does not brown, and cook ~{2%minutes} until a fork goes in with slight resistance. Or add @?bamboo shoots{19%oz}(one can, drained) and heat ~{1%minute}.

Off the heat, stir in the @red bell pepper{1/4}(julienned), then the @Thai basil leaves{1%cup}. Season with more @fish sauce{}.

Serve with @jasmine rice{}.

> The lime leaves flavour the curry but are not for eating. For a stronger curry, fry extra curry paste in a little oil, loosen it with a cup of the sauce, simmer a few minutes and stir it back in. With chicken breast, marinate it in 1 tbsp fish sauce and add it only after the vegetables have cooked a minute; it needs about 2 minutes.
